review_text:
[h2]More of the same[/h2]

[b]Looks like Rebellion did find a recipe for Sniper Elite and every game looks the same thing, despite the years and technology between them. I found Dead Army 4 more enjoyable than this.[/b]

[h3][u]Pros+[/u]:[/h3]
[list]
[*] Nice guns modeling and sound very nice too;
[*] Maps are quite small/medium size but very detailed and beautiful.
[/list]

[h3][u]Cons-[/u]:[/h3]
[list]
[*] Despite guns look and sound, very few are really effective;
[*] AI sometimes will make you laugh;
[*] Two things that I didn't really like: mastering a weapon is still a pain and some character skins (ones I really wanted) require online pvp to get. I hate pvp. I rather pay for them than play pvp to unlock;
[*] Rebellion must have a low budget for voice actors;
[*] DLC rifles are more enjoyable... I wouldn't say "pay to win" but... yeah;
[*] I quite understand this historical fixation with Hitler... but my God, it's enough. Move on, people.
[/list]

Despite beautiful maps and powerful weapons' sounds, it's more of the same (if you are a Sniper Elite/Zombie Army franchise fan): dumb AI, frustrating controls, confusing objectives. Dead Army titles or even Strange Brigade are better than this SE5.

It's a 6/10.

This game is fun.

Pros:
* It has a solid campaign;
* It has nice PvP modes;
* It has nice Coop modes: Campaign coop and Survival (wave survival);
* It has an in-campaign PvP Invasion (Axis player invades campaign players) (My main game mode).
Cons:
* The game DLCs are expensive;
* The Lens glint in PvP (game balancing) is not fun at all. The stealth element we expect from a sniper game is missing.

HEYYYYYY....I've been waiting for this for some time now i'm not gonna explain it all in detail but let me cut to the chase, it's a pretty good game with the story and new AXIS INVASION MODE being pretty cool the game play is decent ( I just wish you could move around more) and the graphics are good as always. 
                { FINAL ---- RATING }

                           (8/10)

2026. Price is 16$ in Kazakhstan, of course worth to buy! It's Metal Gear! :D
BUT!!! Huge BUT. This game has problems in many aspects, I am not enjoying as I would in age of 10-13 ...
Everything is fine in game, but a few things that you might feel:
1. mouse Keyboard is awful, can't make a simple things like jump or move right left in prone;
2. I am playing in Russian where many words still in English, but I saw that in English version a lot of abbreviations: PM PD WD JF BTOW PWB AWLAWIB etc... dumb as hell;
3. plot is for kids. I was about 7 years old when Metal Gear Solid came on market, was fan of MGS 1,2,3 but stopped on MGS 4, I guess because I grew up and hard to follow all of the mental problems in game;
4. YOU can finish game with starter gear. 98% of gear just "why not". 1% of gear to make game easier, 1% of fun RAMBO mode.
5. Main problem of game that it has everything and none of it in perfect quality. Grind, stealth, combat, base development, micro managment simulator, story - everything is .... OK...

I played MGS 5: The Phantom Pain for 4.5 hours and I am done, can't play it anymore.
A stealth action game must give you a motivation to play stealth: strong and smart enemies + atmosphere + exploration + empathy for the protagonist - otherwise, it's just lazy game design, "play stealth because it's a stealth game, and don't ask questions". This game gives zero motivation. Snake is a Rambo, the enemies are dummies, so you could just get your rifle and shoot them all, but even then it would still not be fun because the game is too boring:
* it's just a boring shooter, with bad, Splinter Cell like, shooting mechanics;
* the missions are boring: ride a horse in a dead desert, find, eliminate, "get to da choppa";
* same boring locations are reused for different boring missions;
* the story is for anime girls, written by the Genius himself.
One may disagree and say that "you just didn't play enough, this game will show its full potential after X hours", and I'll say that if you have to suffer for X hours to begin enjoying the game, then the game is not good.

6 years of playing this game (95% single player, not much of a FOB type.)
1 year on PS3;
3 years on PS4;
2 years of modded/retired PC (namely adding difficulty and changing things up for the unexpected.)

[h1] Pros: [/h1]
[list]
[*] engaging gameplay, features one of the best stealth mechanics;
[*] a lot of gun variety;
[*] many approaches for completing objectives are possible;
[*] great soundtrack, voice-acting;
[/list]
[h1] Cons: [/h1]
[list]
[*] incomprehensible plot;
[*] the graphics aren't the greatest—more specifically, the world doesn't feature lots of details it's rather bland;
[*] unfinished;
[/list]

Here's a little list of why you should buy this
Pros:
 - Well optimized, it's really impressive how good fox engine is. Runs smoothly on my GTX 660
 - Full of details all over the game;
 - Good level design for main missions and big outposts in the map, plus various shortcut paths in a open world game;
 - Rich story;
 - Cinematics worthy of an oscar;
 - It's a kojima's game c'mon
Con:
 - Konami
